// expect: compile_error
// expect-error: E492

// Projecting past the end of a tuple — proposal 0185 stage 5.
//
// `p.2` on a pair is now an error. Before stage 5 the receiver of an
// unresolved projection was unified with a *guessed* tuple of
// `max(index + 1, 2)` fresh variables, so this projection made `p` a triple
// instead of being checked against it, and the program compiled with a shape
// no source line asked for.
//
// This file is in working/ deliberately: the rejection is the feature.

fn third(p) { p.2 }

fn main() with IO {
    print(third((1, 2)))
}
